; rungs/respond-defence-strong.eval - the HIGH arm of the `taken` pair.
;
; PARTNER FILE: rungs/respond-defence-weak.eval. THE ONLY LINE THAT MAY DIFFER
; BETWEEN THEM IS THE `spawn` below — x4 here against x2 there. Read that file
; for why this pair is two files while the offence pair is one.
;
; The party is wiped in most samples at x4, which is intended: it is what makes
; `downed` non-zero so that counter is checked too, and `heal` opens each sample
; so the wipe cannot carry into the next one. respond.eval heals at the end so
; the SCRIPT does not finish out of play.

heal
arena open 9 9
freeze off
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 4
tp 14 12
tally reset
step 20
tally
